# Append-only coordination files (kax-conflict-03)
#
# The tool manifest concentrates edits from unrelated tasks into one markdown
# table per topic: 219 commits in the 14 days to 2026-08-08, 95 added rows
# against 22 removed on the three hottest shards alone. Two branches appending
# a row to the same table conflict every time, and the resolution is always
# "take the superset of both rows" — which is exactly what merge=union does.
#
# `tools/ci/pr_watcher.py::_ADDITIVE_PATH_MARKERS` already classified these
# paths as "union-merged coordination files"; until now nothing implemented it.
#
# Verified conflict-free for 2/3/5 concurrent branches in BOTH the local
# `git merge` path and the bare `git merge-tree --write-tree` plumbing a forge
# runs server-side:  python tools/git/manifest_merge_rehearsal.py
#
# Scope note: union is safe here because these files are flat, line-oriented
# tables whose rows are independent. Do NOT extend it to YAML/JSON/Python —
# a union merge there produces duplicate keys or syntactically broken code.
# Its one cost is that a row DELETED on one branch is resurrected when that
# hunk conflicts with an append on another; `coherence_checker`'s manifest
# check reports the byte-identical duplicate rows this leaves behind.
tools/manifest.md merge=union
tools/manifest/*.md merge=union
icdev/tools/manifest.md merge=union
icdev/tools/manifest/*.md merge=union

